{
    "word": "palmyra",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "79733562-c769-30ce-8862-c0f353817399",
                "word": "Palmyra",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "237f2457-df62-3cbc-8136-973b3533e62a",
                        "entry_id": "79733562-c769-30ce-8862-c0f353817399",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An ancient city, an oasis in the Syrian Desert, in present-day central Syria, recorded historically from around 2000 BCE, subsequently subject to various empires and destroyed in 273 CE and again in 1400, when it was reduced to a village."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "00a5f8ed-f13e-4d44-bea2-c37d53d414d0",
                                "sense_id": "237f2457-df62-3cbc-8136-973b3533e62a",
                                "text": "In the mid-fifth century B.C. Herodotus (1:131; 3.8) mentioned the importance of the cult of Al-Ilât, i.e. Allat, in ancient Arabia. Her sanctuary at Palmyra (Pl. XVII), excavated in the 1970s by the Polish mission, is in the neighborhood of the temple of Baal Shamin and lends a special character to the city's western quarter, in which Arab tribes settled during the second century B.C."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b658a7ad-0032-4173-b8c7-d3ce25bb7274",
                                "sense_id": "237f2457-df62-3cbc-8136-973b3533e62a",
                                "text": "The chief man in Palmyra had been charged by Rome to police the trade routes, paying for his militia from his own well-stuffed coffers as befitted a rich man with a civic conscience."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "49756b23-3651-4417-8cad-063b20210cc8",
                                "sense_id": "237f2457-df62-3cbc-8136-973b3533e62a",
                                "text": "Edessa lies just under 300 kilometres north of Palmyra as the crow flies, and its Aramaic dialect, known today as Syriac, is closely related to that of Palmyra."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f53547ee-552b-3b1f-854d-69b9c51a82a4",
                        "entry_id": "79733562-c769-30ce-8862-c0f353817399",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A city, the county seat of Marion County, Missouri, United States."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "40111178-7b83-3cb4-8cf4-90cc7698265b",
                        "entry_id": "79733562-c769-30ce-8862-c0f353817399",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A census-designated place, the county seat of Fluvanna County, Virginia, United States."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
